	<element name="Spellcasting" type="Class Feature" source="System Reference Document 5.1" id="ID_SRD_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_SPELLCASTING">
		<description><p>You have learned to untangle and reshape the fabric of reality in harmony with your wishes and music. Charisma is your spellcasting ability, and you can use a musical instrument as a spellcasting focus.</p></description>
		<sheet display="false" />
	</element>

	<element name="Bardic Inspiration" type="Class Feature" source="System Reference Document 5.1" id="ID_SRD_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_BARDIC_INSPIRATION">
		<description><p>As a bonus action, you can inspire one creature other than yourself within 60 feet who can hear you. It gains a Bardic Inspiration die it can add to one ability check, attack roll or saving throw within the next 10 minutes. You can do this a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum once), regaining uses on a long rest (short rest from 5th level). The die is a d6, becoming a d8 at 5th level, a d10 at 10th and a d12 at 15th.</p></description>
		<sheet>
			<description usage="{{bardic inspiration:count}}/Rest" action="Bonus Action">Grant a d{{bardic inspiration:die}} to a creature within 60 feet.</description>
		</sheet>
		<rules>
			<stat name="bardic inspiration:die" value="6" level="1" />
			<stat name="bardic inspiration:die" value="2" level="5" />
			<stat name="bardic inspiration:die" value="2" level="10" />
			<stat name="bardic inspiration:die" value="2" level="15" />
			<stat name="bardic inspiration:count" value="charisma:modifier" minimum="1" />
		</rules>
	</element>

	<element name="Jack of All Trades" type="Class Feature" source="System Reference Document 5.1" id="ID_SRD_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_JACK_OF_ALL_TRADES">
		<description><p>You can add half your proficiency bonus, rounded down, to any ability check you make that doesn’t already include your proficiency bonus.</p></description>
	</element>

	<element name="Song of Rest" type="Class Feature" source="System Reference Document 5.1" id="ID_SRD_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_SONG_OF_REST">
		<description><p>If you or any friendly creatures who can hear your performance regain hit points by spending Hit Dice at the end of a short rest, each of those creatures regains an extra 1d6 hit points. The die increases to d8 at 9th level, d10 at 13th and d12 at 17th.</p></description>
		<sheet><description>Allies spending Hit Dice during a short rest regain an extra 1d{{song of rest:die}} hit points.</description></sheet>
		<rules>
			<stat name="song of rest:die" value="6" level="2" />
			<stat name="song of rest:die" value="2" level="9" />
			<stat name="song of rest:die" value="2" level="13" />
			<stat name="song of rest:die" value="2" level="17" />
		</rules>
	</element>

	<element name="Expertise" type="Class Feature" source="System Reference Document 5.1" id="ID_SRD_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_EXPERTISE_3">
		<description><p>Choose two of your skill proficiencies. Your proficiency bonus is doubled for any ability check you make that uses either of them. At 10th level you choose two more.</p></description>
		<sheet display="false" />
		<rules>
			<select type="Proficiency" name="Expertise (Bard)" supports="Skill Expertise" number="2" />
		</rules>
	</element>

	<element name="Ability Score Improvement" type="Class Feature" source="System Reference Document 5.1" id="ID_SRD_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_ASI_4">
		<description><p>Increase one ability score by 2 or two ability scores by 1 (maximum 20), or take a feat if your game uses feats.</p></description>
		<sheet display="false" />
		<rules>
			<select type="Class Feature" name="Improvement Option (Bard 4)" supports="Improvement Option" />
		</rules>
	</element>

	<element name="Font of Inspiration" type="Class Feature" source="System Reference Document 5.1" id="ID_SRD_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_FONT_OF_INSPIRATION">
		<description><p>You regain all of your expended uses of Bardic Inspiration when you finish a short or long rest.</p></description>
	</element>

	<element name="Countercharm" type="Class Feature" source="System Reference Document 5.1" id="ID_SRD_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_COUNTERCHARM">
		<description><p>As an action, you can start a performance that lasts until the end of your next turn. During that time, you and friendly creatures within 30 feet have advantage on saving throws against being frightened or charmed.</p></description>
	</element>

